WEBVTT

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:35.220
This is the old castle where Alfred Louis Steinbeck the Third lives.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.220
As you can see, now only the mail is allowed to approach.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.860
Now only Steinbeck and his butler live at the manor,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.950
as Steinbeck does not have a family.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.450
The only outside contact is the mail,

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.950
which the butler sends and receives.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:27.730
English gentleman calling restaurant, 11:10AM on time, without incident.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.990
So, would you like some coffee?

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.870
Ah, of course. If I don't taste it, you won't indulge.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.590
Please.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.420
What is your business with me?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:02.640
The owner of the castle, Steinbeck, is rumoured to be descended from French Royalty.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.430
I do not know if this is true.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.810
Furthermore, his lifestyle is very peculiar.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:12.820
He only goes out once a week in his limousine, driven by his butler.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.110
Their destination is sometimes Royal soirées...

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.410
Sometimes government hosted events.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.790
He is quite something.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.460
Still, if we were to talk about ancestry,

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.290
I would be even higher in rank,

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.800
because my great-grandfather is related to Queen Elizabeth II...

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.630
Ah, but I digress.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.260
Back on topic...

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:46.100
Are you familiar with the agency know as MC-130?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.770
The agency that sells information regarding the health of VIPs all over the world.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.070
Recently the organization has had some trouble with some African nations.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:01.110
Yes... the truth is, the man running MC-130 was a spy for our country.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:06.540
These days we know he is currently selling information to the CIA and other intelligence organizations.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.210
This information includes details pertaining to Her Majesty's government.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.590
And the head of MC-130 is the owner of this castle.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.130
Exactly! As expected of Golgo 13.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:25.260
Because of this, there is a rumour that the Africans aren't the only ones targeting him.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.310
Slowly.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.020
That's why we are using you.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.070
Target.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:42.320
Of course we can eliminate him ourselves, but recently it has become more troublesome.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:49.580
Apparently some countries really need his information.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:58.800
That is why at a recent summit they decided to take him to Switzerland, as a protected leave.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.800
Furthermore, it was decided that the English Government should protect him.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.310
I see. So it must be done by an outsider.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.350
And kept secret.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.310
There are very few people who know about this.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.610
Understood.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.110
I'll do it.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.190
Thank you!

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.650
If you do this, I'll be quite relieved.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.700
The truth is, the castle is quite venerable.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:32.080
In the past, even Queen Elizabeth I stayed at this manor,

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.040
so only true Royalty should be staying in that castle.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:05:02.280
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:13.620
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:25.380
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:31.680
The weak person I was is no more

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:37.270
I decided to just believe

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:44.400
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.240
I go towards you

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.960
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:00.080
I go towards you

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.130
Blown by the wind

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.590
Oh blown

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.730
Steinbeck III

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.410
The castle is like a fortress.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.170
There are surveillance cameras attached everywhere,

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.130
and the windows are bullet-proof glass.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.250
Important doorways are covered with a thick iron plate,

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.380
and security is strict.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.050
Even a mouse would have trouble getting in.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.530
Tomorrow's party at the Earl's mansion is his last event here,

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.120
so it is the best chance for an attack.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.810
English Gentleman to Restaurant.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.940
It is time for the Ark to depart.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.400
The Ark has departed.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.360
We will begin guarding.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.660
Steinbeck's car is also special. It is armoured,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.960
and of course it has bullet-proof glass.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:21.480
No abnormalities. The Ark has arrived safely at the Earl's mansion.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.170
It is nice to see you again, Mrs. Smith.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.340
The pleasure is mine, my Lord Steinbeck.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.720
It is unusual for you to come alone without your husband.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.050
My husband will be along shortly.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.520
Ah, here you are my Lord Chamberlain.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.780
I had heard you were not attending this evening. It is good to see you again.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.360
Actually, I am leaving for Switzerland tomorrow...

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.840
The party is over.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.550
Ark is going home.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.570
The Ark is under attack!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.280
Aim for the muzzle flashes!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.450
Is Lord Steinbeck unharmed?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.790
Yes, he should be.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.960
Watch this area.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:30.370
Sir!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.140
Ah, Sir Richard. Good work.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.260
Are you unharmed?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.140
This car never lets any bullets in.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:50.520
A chance!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.730
Now's your chance! Golgo 13!

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.520
You can hit the target easily...

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.030
What's wrong?!

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.090
Well then Sir Richard, until we leave, I am in your care.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.930
A moment, Lord.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.100
Er...

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:34.810
When might we receive the clinical report about the president that we asked for?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.820
Ah... we will have that for you very soon.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.570
Thank you for your help.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.070
Now! Golgo 13!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:47.700
I'll be off then.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.370
Why...

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.290
By the way...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:58.340
Your report will be delivered before I depart, without fail. Please relax.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.170
Another thing...

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.380
The ulcer in your duodenum is more important, Sir Richard.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.300
Your medical file recently came to my attention.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.890
You should cut back on your coffee and smoking habits.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.270
What are you doing? Get back to your positions!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:17.730
Sir!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:31.740
Why...

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.200
Why didn't you take the shot...

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.750
Golgo 13!

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.470
Someone told me I have to prepare a whole division.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.140
Tanks, helicopters, and even combat jets?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.350
Sounds like you're starting a war.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.440
We have no choice Sylvester.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:07.030
Steinbeck is now an important figure for both the East and the West.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:12.660
England has offered to protect this important figure.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.870
But Richard!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.790
I heard that Steinbeck is working both sides!

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.750
Is this really all right?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.960
It doesn't mean we are giving him to the enemy.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.800
We are bringing him to Switzerland, a neutral country.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.010
Even so, if he goes to Switzerland...

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.140
Well, there's no alternative.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.560
The Western leaders have decided.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.180
Understood. I'll make arrangements.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:38.440
And...

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.980
Hm? What else?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.560
Do you have any coffee?

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.150
I have some prepared already. Help yourself.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:53.620
Honestly, you are not worthy of being called an English Gentleman.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.130
If we change our plans, I'll let you know right away.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.260
Eh?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.760
Drop the mail on purpose?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.350
If that's it, no problem.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.600
No.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.810
What else should I do then?

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.190
The postman will...

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>Accidentally</i> drop his mail.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.150
Accidentally...

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:31.780
So that means not on purpose, but a slip up, eh?

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:47.880
There's only one day left.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.590
Steinbeck is leaving tomorrow.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:53.970
Yeah.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:58.270
And he doesn't leave his manor, so nothing like last night will happen again.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.140
Last day today.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.190
What will you do Golgo 13...

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.940
How will you shoot the target?

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:12.650
Tomorrow the army will be all over this place. The first division will be guarding Steinbeck.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.950
Even you will find those conditions impossible.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.200
What...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.450
What will you do Golgo 13?!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.380
Eleven-fifteen...

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.680
He's five minutes late today.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.580
<i>Accidentally.</i>

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.500
Final delivery is complete.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:16.680
What?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.680
The mail-door hasn't closed...

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.430
Quick! To the castle!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:37.570
What is it?!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.710
Lord Steinbeck! Open the door!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.800
Please open the door!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:54.920
It's him.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.720
Golgo 13 did it,

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.300
but why the butler?

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.060
Lord Richard! What has happened here?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:11.980
We don't know.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:17.070
The postman looked surprised, so we rushed to this location and saw the situation.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.070
So it was him!

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.160
No! I did nothing...

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:24.040
I delivered the mail as usual.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.660
I was waiting for a reply...

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.710
But there was no reaction...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.580
So I looked in the window and already...

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.210
Yes, but...

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.710
But...?

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.260
At that time it looked like you crouched down.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:37.800
Yes,

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:41.350
I dropped a letter, so I picked it up.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.100
It was an accident.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.390
I see, he chose that moment to shoot.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:50.190
Nothing abnormal other than that.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.900
We did a body check. He was carrying no weapons.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.110
However, we are glad that you are safe.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.320
How cruel!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.280
Sir, you have our deepest sympathies.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.140
I... I am sorry to have failed you.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.150
Maybe...

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:51.000
Sir, I am sorry to ask this now,

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.000
but may we have the medical file which we were promised?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.220
As you leave early tomorrow.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.510
Ah, well it has become a bit inconvenient.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:10.020
After I arrive in Switzerland, we will discuss this again.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:13.600
I understand.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:17.150
We will come tomorrow morning to pick you up.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:22.070
Thank... thank you for everything.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:38.300
Now I understand. Steinbeck is the cover. The butler was the real mastermind behind MC-130.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.920
As expected of Golgo 13.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:47.010
I should have suspected after the attack on the car.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:50.430
There was something careless about how Steinbeck got out of the car...

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:51.730
That's it!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:56.770
While the real boss stayed in the car.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.860
The real boss was cowering in the car the whole time!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.070
I'll be off then.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.120
Tomorrow morning.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:15.960
We will send him off amongst the East/West diplomatic corps. It's all settled.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.790
Finally, I can relax.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.710
Even so, foreign policy...

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.880
It's like a duel between a fox and a raccoon-dog.

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.920
As expected from Golgo 13.

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:05.420
Anticipate the deception, then perform the original task.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:07.550
Perfect.

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:39.000
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.550
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:53.430
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:55.770
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:03.860
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:07.780
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:13.030
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:21.250
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.840
It was just a dream

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:29.260
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:34.260
In this calm night

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.510
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:41.650
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:47.610
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:54.070
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:06.170
A cottage by the sea, surrounded by bulletproof glass.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:10.550
The target is the agency of an organ dealer.

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:14.260
He is taking aim from the air.

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:17.930
Adjust the gun-sights only once.

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:25.110
The Glass Fortress

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:20.850
Next time, on Golgo 13:

00:24:21.520 --> 00:24:22.770
The Glass Fortress.

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:27.020
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
